If a clinician continues an opioid-therapy for a patient then the clinician should collaborate with the patient and should evaluate an opioid-continuation-benefit and should evaluate an opioid-continuation-risk and should carefully weigh an opioid-continuation-benefit against an opioid-continuation-risk.
If a clinician increases an opioid-dosage for a patient then the clinician should carefully increase the opioid-dosage.
If a clinician continues an opioid-dosage for a patient then the clinician should carefully continue the opioid-dosage.
If a clinician reduces an opioid-dosage for a patient then the clinician should carefully reduce the opioid-dosage.
